[*] AoU layout : dv/ooo end-to-end out-of-order-by-ID chain (OOO_EN=1).
[*]
[*] Emphasis: the F2 OOO internals, in the order a debug session needs them.
[*]   1. the TB's overtake counters (r_overtakes / b_overtakes) - the run FAILS
[*]      if these stay zero, so they are the first thing to look at;
[*]   2. the TARGET's response-source mux (aou_ooo_resp_src): its one-entry HOLD
[*]      slot (h_valid / h_id / h_timer) is what lets a later different-ID
[*]      response overtake an earlier one;
[*]   3. the INITIATOR's two reorder buffers (u_rob_r for RData, u_rob_w for
[*]      WResp): per-slot occupancy / done vectors, head/tail, and the issue ->
[*]      complete -> output handshakes that restore AXI ordering.
[*]
[*] wave-check: env=ooo
